      "body": "## Motivation\n\n#42588 changed `GPTQXPULinearKernel.process_weights_after_loading` to read `tp_size` from `layer.tp_group.world_size` instead of `get_parallel().tp_size`. `test/registered/xpu/test_xpu_int4_dense.py` still fakes TP with `get_parallel().override(tp_size=...)`. Its bare `LinearBase` has no `tp_group`, so it falls back to the class default `None`, which means `tp_size=1`. As a result:\n\n- `test_gptq_act_order_rejects_split_group_shard` fails: the `tp_size=2` subtest no longer gets the `--tp-size 1` hint. Example failure: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37879819194/job/113656790497\n- `test_gptq_group_aligned_shard_allows_tensor_parallel` still passes, but it now runs at TP=1 instead of TP=2.\n\n#42588 didn't catch this because its XPU job was skipped (no `run-ci` label). The `main` push runs that would have tested it were cancelled by later pushes.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSet `layer.tp_group = SimpleNamespace(world_size=tp_size)` in both places and remove the unused `get_parallel` import. Test-only; no kernel change. The kernel's new lookup is correct for real layers, since every `tp_group` type exposes `world_size`.\n\n## Notes\n\n#34355 carries the same fix for the first spot only. This PR fixes both so it can land on its own and unblock other XPU PRs (e.g. #42048).\n\ncc @ch-wan @YangKai0616\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #37893946349](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37893946349)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37893946367](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37893946367)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #37893946381](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37893946381)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
